      "writtenOn": "2024-04-26T20:25:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You need to define 2 structures, one to hold const data, and the other to hold the mutable state of the driver.\n\nZephyr convention is to use `_config` suffix for the constant data and `_data` for the mutable data.\n\n\n```\nstruct ppm_config {\n    struct device *pdc[num_ports];\n    uint8_t active_port_count;\n};\n\nstruct ppm_data {\n    struct ucsi_ppm_driver *ppm;\n    struct ucsiv3_get_connector_status_data\n\tport_status[NUM_PORTS];\n};\n\nDEVICE_DT_INST_DEFINE(0, \u0026lpm_init, \u0026ppm_data, \u0026ppm_config, POST_KERNEL,\n\t\t      CONFIG_PDC_POWER_MGMT_INIT_PRIORITY, \u0026lpm_drv);\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 72,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "745385b0739c729bf8f3c9f5805b03f125276799",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1911b3ea_184fe256",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ucsi/lpm_driver.c",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 82,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-26T20:25:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These routines should pass `struct device *dev` as the first parameter.\nYou then can access the const and run-time data with\n\n```\nstatic int ucsi_init_ppm(struct device *dev)\n{\n    const struct ppm_config *config \u003d dev-\u003econfig;\n    struct ppm_data *data \u003d dev-\u003edata;\n}\n```\n\nThis will also eliminate the need to include `\tstruct ucsi_pd_device *dev;` in the `struct ucsi_pd_driver` definition.\n\nHowever, I\u0027m not sure the `struct ucsi_pd_driver` is even needed.  There will only ever be one PPM in the system, so passing a handle to the \"PPM instance\" isn\u0027t needed.\n\nThere are instances in Zephyr upstream where this is done.  The `pinctrl_configure_pins()` routine is implemented once per MCU type, so the function definition is overloaded without passing in a `struct device *dev` handle.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 82,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 82,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "745385b0739c729bf8f3c9f5805b03f125276799",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
