      "writtenOn": "2024-04-30T16:05:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think separating `dev` from the driver makes sense but there can be multiple PD drivers in an EC image (ex - we support multiple PDC on a board).\n\nThe reason for keeping the PPM interface as a driver pointer is similar -- some PDC require a full PPM state machine (i.e. PPM common) but others are pass-through. I don\u0027t anticipate having both types of PPMs running at the same time but the driver interface made sense to me as a way to support both.\n\n---\n\nIn any case, removing the dev object from the driver object and making the driver object a const in all cases SGTM.",
